# What does NOT go into the distributed plugin.
#
# This file answers by EXCLUSION rather than by listing what ships, and that is the whole point:
# an enumerated ship list silently omits the next file somebody adds, while an exclusion list
# fails in the safe direction -- a forgotten entry ships something harmless, not a plugin missing
# a class. tools/build-zip.sh reads this, and asserts afterwards that every PHP file atelier.php
# requires is present in the archive.
#
# The distributed plugin is: atelier.php, uninstall.php, readme.txt, LICENSE, and the
# includes/ assets/ blocks/ languages/ directories. Everything below is development apparatus.

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.distignore

# The engineering record. readme.txt is the user-facing documentation; these are not.
AGENTS.md
AGENTS.local.md
CLAUDE.md
CHANGELOG.md
TODO.md
README.md
docs

# Test harness and the fixtures it runs on -- 6.4 MB, none of it reachable at runtime.
tests

# Deployment, the local WordPress builder, and the live-site enumerator.
tools

# Listing images. These belong in SVN under assets/ at the repository root, which is NOT the
# plugin's own assets/ directory and must never be confused with it: anything placed here would
# otherwise be downloaded by every user for no reason.
.wordpress-org

# Deploy scratch, regenerated per release.
urls.txt
*.tsv

# Editor and OS debris
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
node_modules
*.log
